& [ExplosionIdentity] is Phase 2 implementation formation
  + [explosion_uuid] is 52db691b-69c9-404c-9b97-ce5a98ac3f38
  + [boundary] is one live ephemeral read-only Codex turn through stable app-server and stable MCP

& [Fold1Subject] is replace only the mock worker transport
  + [input] is validated CommissionContract, WorkPacket, one exact ProtocolRequest, exact local executables, signed environment, and bounded runtime policy
  + [output] is one observed ProtocolResponse, one schema-bound CandidateArtifact, one event account, and the existing seven-message CycleOutcome
  - never: replace cantor_core semantic authority or deterministic Observer authority

& [Fold2ControlDelineation] is manager-owned process and model-owned inference
  + [manager] launches exact app-server and configures exact Cantor MCP
  + [Codex] performs one inference turn and chooses the one declared tool call
  + [Cantor_MCP] executes the request against exact signed environment
  + [adapter] translates and validates events without inventing semantic results
  + [Observer] reviews the immutable translated result
  - never: give Codex process, shell, file-change, browser, steering, retry, or effect authority

& [Fold3DataDesign] is strict transport evidence
  + [AppServerConfig] is executable paths and digests, expected version, cwd, environment, timeout, line, event, and byte budgets
  + [JsonRpcMessage] is request, response, notification, or server request with bounded identifiers and method names
  + [LiveTurnObservation] is thread, turn, completed item, warning, and terminal state account
  + [McpObservation] is exact server, tool, arguments, result, status, and item identity
  + [LiveCodexCandidate] is schema-bound summary, criteria, proof refs, and requested effects
  + [LiveCodexEvidence] is digests, counts, versions, identities, terminal status, and forbidden-action count

& [Fold4ProtocolGovernance] is fail-closed stable API use
  + [handshake] is initialize response before initialized and any thread request
  + [thread] is ephemeral, read-only, approval never, exact cwd, no experimental capability
  + [turn] is one text assignment, read-only no-network policy, approval never, exact output schema
  + [events] are accepted only within correlation, size, count, time, and state bounds
  + [tool] is exactly one completed MCP call to configured Cantor query_sop
  + [candidate] is exactly one final completed agent message after the tool call
  + [completion] is matching turn/completed with completed status
  + [cleanup] is close stdin then bounded wait and exact child termination if needed

& [Fold5SecurityAndHonesty] is executable and event integrity
  + [executables] are canonical regular non-symlink files matched to expected SHA-256
  + [version] is exact expected codex version before app-server launch
  + [environment] is exact regular file whose digest and request environment digest agree
  + [credential] remains owned by Codex and is never read or returned
  + [forbidden_items] are commandExecution, fileChange, webSearch, dynamicToolCall, collabAgentToolCall, imageGeneration, approval, permission, elicitation, or user input
  + [unexpected_server_request] is denied and faults the cycle
  + [output] is candidate until core protocol verification and Observer review pass

& [Fold6FaultReview] is adversarial
  + [fault] is wrong binary, version, digest, path, environment, handshake, response id, thread id, turn id, event order, item type, tool server, tool name, tool count, tool arguments, tool result, candidate schema, completion status, limit, timeout, EOF, or child exit
  + [prefix] is every translated ecosystem message accepted before the first fault
  + [stderr] is boundedly drained and discarded outside semantic evidence
  - never: retry a model turn automatically or accept a partial final answer

& [Fold7ProofAndGrowthLock] is incremental
  + [deterministic] is fake app-server transcripts for every protocol gate
  + [integration] is a fake child process or transport proving request order and cleanup
  + [live] is one explicit opt-in run against operator-supplied fingerprinted Codex, Cantor MCP, and signed environment
  + [global] is complete workspace gates and evidence manifest
  + [next_locked] is writes, persistent threads, turn steering, approval forwarding, retries, manager iteration, dynamic tools, multiple workers, notifications, and effects
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_for_one_read_only_live_Codex_turn

& [ImplementationReconciliation] is renewed source-processed authority
  + [wire] is nested terminal turn identity, commentary/final phase distinction, and current passive notification set
  + [schema] is provider-compatible strict output plus separate duplicate-set rejection
  + [proof] is exact supervisor-admitted proof-reference equality
  + [candidate] is exact final-message bytes bound by digest and turn identity
  + [live_faults] is old CLI rejection, unsupported schema, and missing-tool final answers preserved as fail-closed evidence
  = [authority] remains narrowed to one separately invoked live turn with no automatic retry
